{"term":"attempt","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:dda29e83e1f154c2e4","definition":"To try.","example":"to attempt an escape from prison","pos":"verb","synonyms":["take a stab at","take a run at","assay","essay","seek"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["apetempt","attemptability","attemptable","attempter","attemptive","unattempted","unattempting","reattempt"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attempt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6a48977116f8a54613","definition":"To try to move, by entreaty, by afflictions, or by temptations; to tempt.","example":"Yet since I see you fearful, that neither my coat, integrity, nor persuasion can with ease attempt you, I will go further than I meant, to pluck all fears out of you.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["take a stab at","take a run at","assay","essay","seek"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["apetempt","attemptability","attemptable","attempter","attemptive","unattempted","unattempting","reattempt"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attempt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f4669f43bc3672a8ab","definition":"To try to win, subdue, or overcome.","example":"one who attempts the virtue of a woman","pos":"verb","synonyms":["take a stab at","take a run at","assay","essay","seek"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["apetempt","attemptability","attemptable","attempter","attemptive","unattempted","unattempting","reattempt"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attempt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:45ca33e1e23ad899dd","definition":"To attack; to make an effort